messages:
Leila (Docs): heads up  docs site build failing for Optimize Toolkit page. the TS example for quant profiles throws a type error during docgen. saw it on staging.
Tom (SDK): ugh. link? I can repro locally with `yarn docs:dev` if you drop the exact error.
Leila (Docs): error from typedoc: `Argument of type '{ profile: string; }' is not assignable to parameter of type 'QuantProfile'`. the snippet uses `profile: 'medium'` instead of the new shape. snippet in question: 
```ts
// current docs snippet
client.optimize.configure({
  model: 'redwood/trim-7b',
  profile: 'medium', // old enum-style profile
  batchPolicy: 'aggressive'
});

// SDK now expects
client.optimize.configure({
  model: 'redwood/trim-7b',
  quantization: { preset: 'medium', dtype: 'int8' },
  batchPolicy: { mode: 'aggressive' }
});
```
Rohan (ML Infra): that rename slipped through when we released quant v0.9. we updated the runtime and TS types but some examples were missed. Changing docs is safe, but we should add a short migration snippet showing the mapping and note about default dtype fallback.
Priya (Product): customers migrating from 0.8 -> 0.9 will definitely hit this. can we include a tiny table in the migration guide: old key -> new shape + recommended dtype? ops teams asked for explicit default values.
Tom (SDK): agreed. I'll open a PR that replaces the shorthand `profile: '...'` with the structured `quantization` object and add a one-line mapping helper in the guide. also will add a small TS helper function so typedoc examples remain clean: 
```ts
function mapProfile(p: 'low'|'medium'|'high') {
  return { preset: p, dtype: p === 'low' ? 'int8' : 'fp16' }
}
```
Leila (Docs): nice. can you also update the python snippet parity? we currently only have py using `quant_profile='medium'` in a couple of playground examples.
Tom (SDK): yep will update both. ps: noticed one sample link in the doc points to `examples/quant-profile.md` on the old `main` branch; the repo default is `master`. will fix links too.
DocBot: docs-ci: build failed on `optimize/quantization.md` -> typedoc error.
Tom (SDK): pushing quick fix PR -> https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/1278 - replaces snippets, adds migration helper, updates link. dropping a note about dtype defaults and runtime fallback behavior.
Rohan (ML Infra): quick FYI on runtime side: if dtype omitted we currently fallback to `fp16` for GPUs and `int8` for quantized CPU builds. maybe add that exact language to avoid confusion. also note perf/cost tradeoffs in the migration note.
Priya (Product): I'll draft the little customer-facing blurb: "Quant presets map to quantization shapes; lower presets reduce memory at the cost of some quality variance. Default dtype varies by deployment (GPU: fp16, CPU: int8)." then attach to PROD-3602.
Leila (Docs): awesome. after PR merges i'll run a docs search for `quant_profile` and `profile:` and open follow-ups for any leftover occurrences. can someone add unit tests for the doc snippets in sample-gen? that would avoid typedoc surprises.
Tom (SDK): good call. i'll add a sample-gen smoke test to ensure TS snippets compile. putting it in the PR.
DocBot: PR 1278 -> CI queued. sample-gen unit tests also queued.
Rohan (ML Infra): after merge i'll coordinate a small runtime note to the console docs explaining the dtype fallback.
Leila (Docs): perfect. thanks everyone. leaving this thread; will circle back if CI still complains. :sparkles:
